#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Label Printer Tester - test-print Zebra and Dymo label printers on Ubuntu.

One window: plug a printer in, it shows up in the list, pick it, print.
  Zebra: talks to the printer directly over USB (/dev/usb/lp*): factory reset,
         calibration, label size detection, full-size ZPL/EPL test labels.
  Dymo:  installs the Dymo driver if needed, sets the printer up in CUPS with
         the right driver, prints a full-size test label for the chosen labels.
  Tools: clean up old printers that aren't connected any more.
"""

